  "question": {
    "text": "A solution of aluminium chloride is electrolysed for 30 minutes using a current of 2 A . The amount of the aluminium deposited at the cathode is\n[Given : molar mass of aluminium and chlorine are $27 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ and $35.5 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ respectively. Faraday constant $\\left.=96500 \\mathrm{C} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9BIjF",
      "text": "1.660 g",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PWQdi",
      "text": "0.336 g",
      "image": null,
